\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Schematic of a server tick (illustrative timings, not measured data). Each tick the server receives client input, updates the world, and sends a snapshot; at 20~Hz it has 50~ms for all of it. If the work per tick grows with the number of clients and passes 50~ms, ticks start late, the effective tick rate falls ($1000/80=12.5$~Hz in panel~C) and clients get fewer, later snapshots.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tickvisual}{{1}{2}{Schematic of a server tick (illustrative timings, not measured data). Each tick the server receives client input, updates the world, and sends a snapshot; at 20~Hz it has 50~ms for all of it. If the work per tick grows with the number of clients and passes 50~ms, ticks start late, the effective tick rate falls ($1000/80=12.5$~Hz in panel~C) and clients get fewer, later snapshots}{figure.1}{}}
